    "tool_calls": 31,
    "summary": "Fixed the wchunk package to match the actual binary format found in the sample files. Key changes:\n\n1. **header.py**: Changed record count from big-endian u32 to little-endian u32 (`struct.pack(\"<I\", ...)` instead of `\">I\"`).\n\n2. **codec.py**: Completely rewrote record encoding/decoding:\n   - Records use fixed-width fields: tag(u16 LE) + size(u16 LE) + payload, replacing the varint encoding\n   - Each record is padded to 8-byte boundary\n   - Footer is 6 bytes: CRC32_LE(4) + tag_sum_LE(2), where tag_sum is the sum of all tags mod 2^16\n   - FOOTER_SIZE changed from 4 to 6\n   - Added tag sum verification in unpack()\n\n3. **crc.py**: Fixed compute_crc to return standard CRC-32 (`zlib.crc32(data) & 0xFFFFFFFF`) instead of the broken `zlib.crc32(data) ^ 0xFFFFFFFF`.\n\n4. **stream.py**: Updated iter_records to use fixed-width u16 LE fields with 8-byte record alignment, handle 6-byte footer (CRC + tag sum), and maintain incremental CRC computation over header + records including padding.\n\nThe for",
    "changed_workspace": true
